  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A freshly prepared radioactive source of half life <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> hours <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math> minutes emits radiation which is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn></math> times the permissible safe level. The minimum time, after which it would be possible to work safely with source, will be _____ hours.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></math>&nbsp;minutes,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is the safe limit.</p><p>Using radioactive decay law relation,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></msup></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;the minimum time in hours after which it would be possible to work safely with source.</p><p>Putting the values, we have&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math>&nbsp;hours</p></blockquote>",
